From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: skyjet18 <57456827+skyjet18@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:30:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 42/49] fixed segfault in hls subtitle handling

Ported to FFmpeg 9.0.2 from 0012-fixed-segfault-in-hls-subtitle-handling.patch
(0010 of the FFmpeg 8.0 set, used as base). Applied unchanged (offset
only). 9.0.2 already closes a stale input when the subtitle context is
gone, so this only simplifies the condition; kept for parity with the
8.0 set.
---
 libavformat/hls.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
index 6b3e7673..234fe9e0 100644
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -1986,7 +1986,7 @@ restart:
     if (v->input && !v->ctx)
         ff_format_io_close(v->parent, &v->input);
 
-    if (!v->input && !v->ctx) {
+    if (!v->ctx) {
         ret = init_subtitle_context(v);
         if (ret < 0)
             return ret;
